{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014PFWSt37kcwfrfYbqwP1vx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: \"放弃 'universal depth signal' 叙事，转向 'architecture-conditional depth response'。核心贡献变为：识别 depth signal 存在/崩溃的条件，以及 signal 缺失本身作为生成器 fingerprint 的二阶信号。仍冲 EMNLP，定位为 negative/characterization paper。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"feature_ablation_and_trend\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"MVP Pythia-only 数据上的特征消融 + 趋势分析 + perplexity 预验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      full_macro_f1: 0.81\n      reference_only_f1: 0.68\n      surface_only_f1: 0.77\n      ref_vs_surf_bootstrap_p: 0.003\n      h2_features: \"entropy_mean (slope=-0.42, R²=0.88), ttr (slope=-0.11, R²=0.91), hapax_ratio (slope=-0.14, R²=0.93)\"\n      h1_features: \"tail_decay (slope=-0.02, R²=0.15), entropy_std (slope=+0.01, R²=0.08), entropy_max (slope=-0.06, R²=0.31), entropy_min (slope=-0.09, R²=0.42)\"\n      entropy_min_ambiguous: true\n      median_ppl_by_depth: \"13.2, 5.1, 3.2, 2.3, 1.8\"\n      ppl_depth_spearman: -0.95\n    result_rationale: \"Pythia-410M reference + Pythia-2.8B generator 是 same-family 最佳条件，即使在 worst 档位下初始 MVP 数据仍然能看到 depth signal。问题不在这里暴露——surface features（TTR/hapax）占主导（0.77 vs ref-only 0.68）暗示 depth signal 主要来自 vocabulary impoverishment 而非深层 distributional structure。entropy_min 的 R²=0.42 处于模糊地带（不完全 stationary），为后续 cross-family 失败埋下伏笔：这种 intermediate behavior 说明 drifting/stationary 分界在不同架构下可能不一致。Reference features 弱于 surface 是 worst 档早期信号——如果 dual dynamics 是 robust phenomenon，reference features 应至少持平。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Feature Ablation (5-fold CV, Pythia-2.8B only)\"\n        columns: [\"Feature Set\", \"Macro F1\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Full 7-feature\", 0.81, \"[0.79, 0.83]\"]\n          - [\"Surface only (TTR + hapax)\", 0.77, \"[0.75, 0.79]\"]\n          - [\"Reference only (5 entropy feats)\", 0.68, \"[0.65, 0.71]\"]\n          - [\"entropy_mean alone\", 0.64, \"[0.61, 0.67]\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Linear Trend per Feature (depth 0-4)\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"Slope\", \"R²\", \"Classification\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"hapax_ratio\", -0.14, 0.93, \"Drifting\"]\n          - [\"ttr\", -0.11, 0.91, \"Drifting\"]\n          - [\"entropy_mean\", -0.42, 0.88, \"Drifting\"]\n          - [\"entropy_min\", -0.09, 0.42, \"Ambiguous\"]\n          - [\"entropy_max\", -0.06, 0.31, \"Stationary\"]\n          - [\"tail_decay\", -0.02, 0.15, \"Stationary\"]\n          - [\"entropy_std\", 0.01, 0.08, \"Stationary\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: 7 个特征 mean±std across depth 0-4。hapax/ttr/entropy_mean 呈明显单调下降，entropy_std/tail_decay 基本平坦，entropy_min 呈弱下降趋势（R²=0.42），预示跨架构不一致的隐患。\"\n    analysis: \"Initial signal looks promising on same-family data but two warning signs: (1) surface features dominate reference features by 9pp, suggesting vocabulary impoverishment is the primary signal carrier, not distributional structure shifts; (2) entropy_min sits in an ambiguous zone. In worst tier these are early indicators that the 'dual dynamics' framework is architecture-specific — it cleanly separates on Pythia but may not generalize. Proceed to plan_002 but with lowered expectations for cross-family transfer.\"\n\n  - name: \"cross_generator_evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"5 生成器 (Pythia-2.8B/1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B) LOGO 交叉验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 18200\n      logo_avg_macro_f1_3class: 0.72\n      logo_avg_binary_f1: 0.67\n      logo_per_generator:\n        pythia-2.8b: {3class: 0.82, binary: 0.78}\n        pythia-1b: {3class: 0.84, binary: 0.80}\n        olmo-2-1b: {3class: 0.63, binary: 0.58}\n        qwen3-1.7b: {3class: 0.67, binary: 0.62}\n        qwen3-0.6b: {3class: 0.64, binary: 0.57}\n      per_gen_f1_std: 0.11\n      leave_one_family_out:\n        held_out_pythia: 0.79\n        held_out_olmo: 0.58\n        held_out_qwen: 0.60\n      ablation_full_f1: 0.72\n      ablation_surface_only_f1: 0.70\n      ablation_reference_only_f1: 0.61\n      mcnemar_full_vs_surface_p: 0.12\n      generators_below_060_binary: 2\n      spearman_by_generator:\n        pythia-2.8b: {entropy_mean: -0.61, ttr: -0.58, hapax: -0.63}\n        pythia-1b: {entropy_mean: -0.55, ttr: -0.54, hapax: -0.60}\n        olmo-2-1b: {entropy_mean: -0.22, ttr: -0.35, hapax: -0.38}\n        qwen3-1.7b: {entropy_mean: -0.31, ttr: -0.40, hapax: -0.43}\n        qwen3-0.6b: {entropy_mean: -0.18, ttr: -0.33, hapax: -0.36}\n      feature_direction_inconsistency: \"OLMo entropy_mean correlation weakly negative (-0.22) while Pythia strongly negative (-0.61); effect size ratio 2.8x\"\n    result_rationale: \"Worst 档核心假设在此暴露：2+ 新家族 held-out F1 < 0.60。Pythia 家族内 transfer 良好（两个 Pythia 模型互相泄露 inductive bias），但 OLMo 和 Qwen 家族 held-out 时 binary F1 掉到 0.57-0.58。原因：(1) OLMo 的 training recipe（Dolma corpus + unique LR schedule）产生不同的 token frequency distribution，导致 Pythia-410M reference model 的 entropy features 对 OLMo 生成文本的 depth drift 不敏感——entropy_mean 的 Spearman 仅 -0.22（vs Pythia -0.61），effect size 缩小 2.8x；(2) Qwen tokenizer 完全不同（byte-level BPE vs Pythia GPT-NeoX tokenizer），surface features（TTR/hapax）的计算基于不同 vocabulary space，导致跨家族 surface feature 分布 mismatch；(3) full vs surface-only 差距仅 2pp（0.72 vs 0.70），McNemar p=0.12 不显著——7-feature ensemble 在这个场景下不优于简单 surface features，印证 'seven_feat_vs_best_baseline_pp: [0, 2.0]' 的 worst 预期。per_gen_f1_std = 0.11 远高于 'universal' 叙事所需的一致性。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LOGO Cross-Generator Results\"\n        columns: [\"Held-out Generator\", \"3-class F1\", \"Binary F1\", \"Family\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pythia-2.8B\", 0.82, 0.78, \"Pythia\"]\n          - [\"Pythia-1B\", 0.84, 0.80, \"Pythia\"]\n          - [\"OLMo-2-1B\", 0.63, 0.58, \"OLMo\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-1.7B\", 0.67, 0.62, \"Qwen\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-0.6B\", 0.64, 0.57, \"Qwen\"]\n          - [\"**Average**\", \"**0.72**\", \"**0.67**\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Feature Ablation (5-gen LOGO)\"\n        columns: [\"Feature Set\", \"Avg LOGO F1\", \"p vs Full\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Full 7-feature\", 0.72, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Surface only\", 0.70, \"0.12 (NS)\"]\n          - [\"Reference only\", 0.61, \"<0.001\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Spearman ρ (entropy_mean vs depth) by Generator\"\n        columns: [\"Generator\", \"ρ\", \"p-value\", \"Effect interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pythia-2.8B\", -0.61, \"<0.001\", \"Strong\"]\n          - [\"Pythia-1B\", -0.55, \"<0.001\", \"Moderate-Strong\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-1.7B\", -0.31, \"<0.001\", \"Weak-Moderate\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-0.6B\", -0.18, \"<0.001\", \"Weak\"]\n          - [\"OLMo-2-1B\", -0.22, \"<0.001\", \"Weak\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2: Per-generator LOGO F1 bar chart with 95% CI error bars. Clear bimodal pattern: Pythia family (0.78-0.80) vs non-Pythia (0.57-0.62). CI bars for OLMo/Qwen overlap with 0.50 random baseline lower bound.\"\n      - \"Fig 3: entropy_mean trend lines (depth 0-4) for each generator. Pythia lines steep and parallel; OLMo nearly flat; Qwen shows weak inconsistent slope. Visual evidence of architecture-conditional response.\"\n    analysis: \"Universality claim collapses. The 2-tier pattern (Pythia strong, others weak) indicates depth signal is not an intrinsic property of recursive generation but depends on architecture/training-data alignment with the reference model AND possibly on the generator's own sampling dynamics. Two interpretations: (A) reference model mismatch — Pythia-410M is a poor scorer for non-Pythia text, inflating entropy baseline and suppressing drift measurement; (B) genuine architecture difference — some models produce more uniform token distributions at every depth, compressing the dynamic range for drift detection. Plan_003 (cross-family reference) will disambiguate. If (A), using OLMo/Qwen reference fixes it; if (B), the signal genuinely doesn't exist for these families. In worst tier, we expect (B) to dominate. Narrative must pivot to conditional claims.\"\n\n  - name: \"paraphrastic_comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Paraphrasing chains vs continuation chains 直接对比，测试 attractor convergence 理论\"\n    expected_results:\n      paraphrastic_3class_f1: 0.60\n      paraphrastic_binary_f1: 0.53\n      continuation_3class_f1: 0.72\n      continuation_binary_f1: 0.67\n      f1_3class_delta: -0.12\n      spearman_entropy_mean_para: 0.15\n      spearman_entropy_mean_cont: -0.42\n      spearman_ttr_para: 0.31\n      spearman_ttr_cont: -0.48\n      spearman_hapax_para: 0.28\n      spearman_hapax_cont: -0.51\n      cross_transfer_para_to_cont_f1: 0.38\n      cross_transfer_cont_to_para_f1: 0.42\n      depth_retention_para: 0.92\n      depth_retention_cont: 0.83\n      para_attractor_convergence_gen3: true\n      n_paraphrastic: 4800\n      n_continuation: 4600\n    result_rationale: \"Worst 档下，paraphrastic chains 呈现 attractor convergence 预期行为：entropy_mean Spearman 仅 +0.15（趋于 neutral/轻微 positive，即 paraphrasing 使 perplexity 略微上升后稳定）。但 continuation chains 也弱于 expected——在 5-gen pooled data 上 Spearman 仅 -0.42（而非 best 档的 -0.65+），因为 non-Pythia generators 拉低了整体 correlation。关键是 sign reversal：paraphrastic 正相关 vs continuation 负相关，但 effect size 都不大。Cross-transfer F1 极低（0.38-0.42），说明两种 chain 类型的 feature space 几乎不重叠——这在 worst 档是问题而非 feature，因为它意味着 'depth signal' 高度 task-specific，不是一个 unified phenomenon。Depth retention 0.92 for para（高于 continuation 的 0.83）也 counterintuitive：paraphrasing 保留更多 chains 但 signal 更弱，说明 chain stability ≠ signal strength。Attractor convergence 在 gen-3 后明显——para chains 的 feature 分布停止变化。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Paraphrastic vs Continuation Depth Signal\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Paraphrastic\", \"Continuation\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"3-class LOGO F1\", 0.60, 0.72, -0.12]\n          - [\"Binary LOGO F1\", 0.53, 0.67, -0.14]\n          - [\"ρ(entropy_mean, depth)\", \"+0.15\", \"-0.42\", \"sign reversed\"]\n          - [\"ρ(TTR, depth)\", \"+0.31\", \"-0.48\", \"sign reversed\"]\n          - [\"ρ(hapax, depth)\", \"+0.28\", \"-0.51\", \"sign reversed\"]\n          - [\"Depth retention (gen4/gen0)\", 0.92, 0.83, \"+0.09\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-transfer LOGO F1\"\n        columns: [\"Train on\", \"Test on\", \"F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Continuation\", \"Continuation\", 0.72]\n          - [\"Paraphrastic\", \"Paraphrastic\", 0.60]\n          - [\"Continuation → Para\", \"Paraphrastic\", 0.42]\n          - [\"Para → Continuation\", \"Continuation\", 0.38]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: Parallel feature trajectories (depth 0-4) for para vs cont chains. Continuation lines drift downward (vocabulary impoverishment); paraphrastic lines converge to plateau by gen-3 (attractor behavior). 但两者 effect sizes 都小于 expected。\"\n    analysis: \"Sign reversal confirms theoretically expected behavior (paraphrasing → attractor convergence, continuation → monotonic drift), but under worst tier the effect sizes are underwhelming for both types. Paraphrastic binary F1=0.53 is near random — essentially unclassifiable beyond gen-0 vs rest. Continuation is better but still weak (0.67 binary). The low cross-transfer (0.38-0.42) means there's no unified 'depth signal' that works across chain types — each requires its own model. For EMNLP reframing: this SUPPORTS the 'architecture-conditional' narrative because it shows depth signal properties depend on the specific generation process (paraphrasing vs continuation vs architecture), not just depth itself. The attractor convergence finding is a positive contribution to theory validation even in worst case.\"\n\n  - name: \"finer_grained_ordinal\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"5-class ordinal classification (gen-0 through gen-4) 测试更细粒度深度估计\"\n    expected_results:\n      5class_macro_f1: 0.38\n      5class_f1_std: 0.04\n      5class_accuracy: 0.42\n      5class_mae: 0.95\n      3class_macro_f1: 0.72\n      delta_5class_vs_3class: -0.34\n      per_class_f1:\n        depth_0: 0.85\n        depth_1: 0.45\n        depth_2: 0.22\n        depth_3: 0.18\n        depth_4: 0.20\n      confusion_concentration: \"gen2/gen3/gen4 互相混淆，占 confusion matrix off-diagonal 的 72%\"\n      ordinal_methods:\n        CORAL: 0.36\n        frank_hall: 0.39\n        xgboost: 0.38\n      depth_2_3_separability: \"Cohen's d = 0.08 (entropy_mean), 0.12 (hapax_ratio) — 几乎不可分\"\n      per_family_5class:\n        pythia_held_out: 0.48\n        olmo_held_out: 0.28\n        qwen_held_out: 0.31\n    result_rationale: \"Worst 档下，5-class 在 pooled 5-gen data 上 macro F1 仅 0.38，接近 5-class random baseline（0.20）但仍显著高于 chance。核心问题：depth 2/3/4 几乎不可分（per-class F1 0.18-0.22）。原因是双重的：(1) depth drift 在多数生成器（OLMo/Qwen）上本身就弱，加上 (2) gen-2 到 gen-4 之间的 feature 增量极小（Cohen's d < 0.12），即使在 Pythia 上也进入 plateau。只有 gen-0 可靠分类（F1=0.85），gen-1 中等（0.45）——这本质上是 binary detection（gen-0 vs rest）在 5-class 框架中的残影。OLMo/Qwen held-out 时 5-class F1 掉到 0.28-0.31（接近 random），进一步说明 fine-grained 深度估计只在特定架构下可行。Ordinal-specific methods（CORAL/Frank-Hall）无优势，因为 underlying signal 本身不存在于 deep depths。3-class（0.72）远优于 5-class（0.38），但 delta = 34pp 说明 3-class 的性能也主要来自 gen-0 classification 而非真正的 ordinal discrimination。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Ordinal Classification Results\"\n        columns: [\"Granularity\", \"Method\", \"Macro F1\", \"MAE\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"3-class\", \"XGBoost\", 0.72, 0.31]\n          - [\"5-class\", \"XGBoost\", 0.38, 0.95]\n          - [\"5-class\", \"CORAL\", 0.36, 0.98]\n          - [\"5-class\", \"Frank-Hall\", 0.39, 0.92]\n      - name: \"Table: 5-class Per-depth F1\"\n        columns: [\"Depth\", \"F1\", \"Support\", \"Most confused with\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"gen-0\", 0.85, 4950, \"gen-1 (10%)\"]\n          - [\"gen-1\", 0.45, 4900, \"gen-2 (28%)\"]\n          - [\"gen-2\", 0.22, 4600, \"gen-3 (35%), gen-1 (22%)\"]\n          - [\"gen-3\", 0.18, 4200, \"gen-2 (33%), gen-4 (30%)\"]\n          - [\"gen-4\", 0.20, 3800, \"gen-3 (38%), gen-2 (21%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: 5×5 Confusion matrix heatmap。gen-0 行几乎全在对角线；gen-2/3/4 行呈均匀分布，对角线无明显 peak。直观展示 depth > 1 的不可分性。\"\n      - \"Fig 6: Feature distributions (violin plots) by depth 0-4, split by generator family。Pythia violins 逐层分离；OLMo/Qwen violins 从 depth-1 开始完全重叠。\"\n    analysis: \"5-class ordinal is infeasible in worst tier. The signal exists primarily at the gen-0/gen-1 boundary and rapidly degrades. This is actually informative for the reframed paper: it establishes an empirical ceiling on depth resolution (≤3 classes) that's architecture-dependent. For Pythia-family generators where signal is strong, 4-class might work; for others, even binary (gen-1 vs gen-2+) is near chance. The 'conditions under which depth signal emerges vs collapses' framing gains direct evidence: depth granularity is architecture-conditional, not a universal property of recursive generation. Report as structured negative finding.\"\n\n  - name: \"end_to_end_classifier\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"QLoRA fine-tuned Qwen3.5-0.8B 端到端深度分类，对比 handcrafted features\"\n    expected_results:\n      5class_macro_f1: 0.44\n      5class_f1_std: 0.02\n      3class_macro_f1: 0.76\n      3class_f1_std: 0.01\n      per_class_f1:\n        gen0: 0.95\n        gen1: 0.62\n        gen2: 0.30\n        gen3: 0.22\n        gen4: 0.11\n      vs_xgboost_5class_delta_pp: \"+6.0\"\n      vs_xgboost_3class_delta_pp: \"+4.0\"\n      logo_generalization:\n        pythia_held_out: 0.52\n        olmo_held_out: 0.35\n        qwen_held_out: 0.38\n      overfitting_gap: 0.18\n      train_f1: 0.62\n      val_f1: 0.44\n      runtime_hours: 14\n      model: \"Qwen3-0.6B-Base\"\n      method: \"QLoRA rank-16\"\n    result_rationale: \"E2E model 在 5-class 上优于 XGBoost（0.44 vs 0.38，+6pp），因为 learned representations 能捕获 handcrafted features 遗漏的 subtle patterns（如 attention pattern shifts、specific n-gram frequency changes）。但绝对性能仍然很差（0.44），且 overfitting 严重（train 0.62 vs val 0.44，gap=18pp）——模型学到了 generator-specific artifacts 而非 generalizable depth signal。LOGO generalization 更加灾难性：held-out Pythia F1=0.52，OLMo/Qwen 仅 0.35-0.38。这说明 E2E model 学到的不是 'depth signal' 而是 'generator fingerprint + depth 交互'——它在训练集内的 generator 上过拟合。3-class（0.76）优于 XGBoost（0.72）但差距不大（+4pp），且同样来自 gen-0 classification。在 worst 档下，E2E 的相对优势说明确实有 beyond-handcrafted-features 的信号存在，但这些信号 generator-specific、不泛化，支持 'architecture-conditional' reframing。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: E2E vs Handcrafted Features\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"5-class F1\", \"3-class F1\", \"LOGO 5-class F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"XGBoost 7-feature\", 0.38, 0.72, 0.34]\n          - [\"QLoRA Qwen3-0.6B\", 0.44, 0.76, 0.38]\n          - [\"Delta\", \"+0.06\", \"+0.04\", \"+0.04\"]\n      - name: \"Table: QLoRA LOGO Per-family Held-out\"\n        columns: [\"Held-out Family\", \"5-class F1\", \"Overfitting gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pythia (2.8B+1B)\", 0.52, 0.10]\n          - [\"OLMo-2-1B\", 0.35, 0.27]\n          - [\"Qwen (1.7B+0.6B)\", 0.38, 0.24]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: Learning curves (train/val F1 vs epoch). Val F1 plateaus at epoch 3 while train continues climbing → clear overfitting signal. Val F1 on held-out families (OLMo/Qwen) peaks at epoch 2 then degrades.\"\n    analysis: \"E2E model provides modest improvement over handcrafted features but does not solve the fundamental problem: depth signal for non-Pythia architectures is weak or absent. The overfitting pattern (generator-specific memorization) is actually diagnostic evidence for the reframed paper: it shows that whatever distinguishes depths for a given generator is not transferable across architectures. This supports the 'architecture-conditional depth response' thesis — each model family has its own depth signature (if any), and there is no universal learned representation of 'depth'. For the paper: report as supplementary evidence that neither handcrafted nor learned features achieve universal depth discrimination, strengthening the conditional-claim reframing.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28762,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28762},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b710055-31f3-4d1c-83bc-cef72e560573","uuid":"211efac0-ed76-4f0f-91bd-b2bb82b75faa"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":180430,"duration_api_ms":182005,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: \"放弃 'universal depth signal' 叙事，转向 'architecture-conditional depth response'。核心贡献变为：识别 depth signal 存在/崩溃的条件，以及 signal 缺失本身作为生成器 fingerprint 的二阶信号。仍冲 EMNLP，定位为 negative/characterization paper。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"feature_ablation_and_trend\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"MVP Pythia-only 数据上的特征消融 + 趋势分析 + perplexity 预验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      full_macro_f1: 0.81\n      reference_only_f1: 0.68\n      surface_only_f1: 0.77\n      ref_vs_surf_bootstrap_p: 0.003\n      h2_features: \"entropy_mean (slope=-0.42, R²=0.88), ttr (slope=-0.11, R²=0.91), hapax_ratio (slope=-0.14, R²=0.93)\"\n      h1_features: \"tail_decay (slope=-0.02, R²=0.15), entropy_std (slope=+0.01, R²=0.08), entropy_max (slope=-0.06, R²=0.31), entropy_min (slope=-0.09, R²=0.42)\"\n      entropy_min_ambiguous: true\n      median_ppl_by_depth: \"13.2, 5.1, 3.2, 2.3, 1.8\"\n      ppl_depth_spearman: -0.95\n    result_rationale: \"Pythia-410M reference + Pythia-2.8B generator 是 same-family 最佳条件，即使在 worst 档位下初始 MVP 数据仍然能看到 depth signal。问题不在这里暴露——surface features（TTR/hapax）占主导（0.77 vs ref-only 0.68）暗示 depth signal 主要来自 vocabulary impoverishment 而非深层 distributional structure。entropy_min 的 R²=0.42 处于模糊地带（不完全 stationary），为后续 cross-family 失败埋下伏笔：这种 intermediate behavior 说明 drifting/stationary 分界在不同架构下可能不一致。Reference features 弱于 surface 是 worst 档早期信号——如果 dual dynamics 是 robust phenomenon，reference features 应至少持平。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Feature Ablation (5-fold CV, Pythia-2.8B only)\"\n        columns: [\"Feature Set\", \"Macro F1\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Full 7-feature\", 0.81, \"[0.79, 0.83]\"]\n          - [\"Surface only (TTR + hapax)\", 0.77, \"[0.75, 0.79]\"]\n          - [\"Reference only (5 entropy feats)\", 0.68, \"[0.65, 0.71]\"]\n          - [\"entropy_mean alone\", 0.64, \"[0.61, 0.67]\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Linear Trend per Feature (depth 0-4)\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"Slope\", \"R²\", \"Classification\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"hapax_ratio\", -0.14, 0.93, \"Drifting\"]\n          - [\"ttr\", -0.11, 0.91, \"Drifting\"]\n          - [\"entropy_mean\", -0.42, 0.88, \"Drifting\"]\n          - [\"entropy_min\", -0.09, 0.42, \"Ambiguous\"]\n          - [\"entropy_max\", -0.06, 0.31, \"Stationary\"]\n          - [\"tail_decay\", -0.02, 0.15, \"Stationary\"]\n          - [\"entropy_std\", 0.01, 0.08, \"Stationary\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: 7 个特征 mean±std across depth 0-4。hapax/ttr/entropy_mean 呈明显单调下降，entropy_std/tail_decay 基本平坦，entropy_min 呈弱下降趋势（R²=0.42），预示跨架构不一致的隐患。\"\n    analysis: \"Initial signal looks promising on same-family data but two warning signs: (1) surface features dominate reference features by 9pp, suggesting vocabulary impoverishment is the primary signal carrier, not distributional structure shifts; (2) entropy_min sits in an ambiguous zone. In worst tier these are early indicators that the 'dual dynamics' framework is architecture-specific — it cleanly separates on Pythia but may not generalize. Proceed to plan_002 but with lowered expectations for cross-family transfer.\"\n\n  - name: \"cross_generator_evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"5 生成器 (Pythia-2.8B/1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B) LOGO 交叉验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 18200\n      logo_avg_macro_f1_3class: 0.72\n      logo_avg_binary_f1: 0.67\n      logo_per_generator:\n        pythia-2.8b: {3class: 0.82, binary: 0.78}\n        pythia-1b: {3class: 0.84, binary: 0.80}\n        olmo-2-1b: {3class: 0.63, binary: 0.58}\n        qwen3-1.7b: {3class: 0.67, binary: 0.62}\n        qwen3-0.6b: {3class: 0.64, binary: 0.57}\n      per_gen_f1_std: 0.11\n      leave_one_family_out:\n        held_out_pythia: 0.79\n        held_out_olmo: 0.58\n        held_out_qwen: 0.60\n      ablation_full_f1: 0.72\n      ablation_surface_only_f1: 0.70\n      ablation_reference_only_f1: 0.61\n      mcnemar_full_vs_surface_p: 0.12\n      generators_below_060_binary: 2\n      spearman_by_generator:\n        pythia-2.8b: {entropy_mean: -0.61, ttr: -0.58, hapax: -0.63}\n        pythia-1b: {entropy_mean: -0.55, ttr: -0.54, hapax: -0.60}\n        olmo-2-1b: {entropy_mean: -0.22, ttr: -0.35, hapax: -0.38}\n        qwen3-1.7b: {entropy_mean: -0.31, ttr: -0.40, hapax: -0.43}\n        qwen3-0.6b: {entropy_mean: -0.18, ttr: -0.33, hapax: -0.36}\n      feature_direction_inconsistency: \"OLMo entropy_mean correlation weakly negative (-0.22) while Pythia strongly negative (-0.61); effect size ratio 2.8x\"\n    result_rationale: \"Worst 档核心假设在此暴露：2+ 新家族 held-out F1 < 0.60。Pythia 家族内 transfer 良好（两个 Pythia 模型互相泄露 inductive bias），但 OLMo 和 Qwen 家族 held-out 时 binary F1 掉到 0.57-0.58。原因：(1) OLMo 的 training recipe（Dolma corpus + unique LR schedule）产生不同的 token frequency distribution，导致 Pythia-410M reference model 的 entropy features 对 OLMo 生成文本的 depth drift 不敏感——entropy_mean 的 Spearman 仅 -0.22（vs Pythia -0.61），effect size 缩小 2.8x；(2) Qwen tokenizer 完全不同（byte-level BPE vs Pythia GPT-NeoX tokenizer），surface features（TTR/hapax）的计算基于不同 vocabulary space，导致跨家族 surface feature 分布 mismatch；(3) full vs surface-only 差距仅 2pp（0.72 vs 0.70），McNemar p=0.12 不显著——7-feature ensemble 在这个场景下不优于简单 surface features，印证 'seven_feat_vs_best_baseline_pp: [0, 2.0]' 的 worst 预期。per_gen_f1_std = 0.11 远高于 'universal' 叙事所需的一致性。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LOGO Cross-Generator Results\"\n        columns: [\"Held-out Generator\", \"3-class F1\", \"Binary F1\", \"Family\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pythia-2.8B\", 0.82, 0.78, \"Pythia\"]\n          - [\"Pythia-1B\", 0.84, 0.80, \"Pythia\"]\n          - [\"OLMo-2-1B\", 0.63, 0.58, \"OLMo\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-1.7B\", 0.67, 0.62, \"Qwen\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-0.6B\", 0.64, 0.57, \"Qwen\"]\n          - [\"**Average**\", \"**0.72**\", \"**0.67**\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Feature Ablation (5-gen LOGO)\"\n        columns: [\"Feature Set\", \"Avg LOGO F1\", \"p vs Full\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Full 7-feature\", 0.72, \"—\"]\n          - [\"Surface only\", 0.70, \"0.12 (NS)\"]\n          - [\"Reference only\", 0.61, \"<0.001\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Spearman ρ (entropy_mean vs depth) by Generator\"\n        columns: [\"Generator\", \"ρ\", \"p-value\", \"Effect interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pythia-2.8B\", -0.61, \"<0.001\", \"Strong\"]\n          - [\"Pythia-1B\", -0.55, \"<0.001\", \"Moderate-Strong\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-1.7B\", -0.31, \"<0.001\", \"Weak-Moderate\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-0.6B\", -0.18, \"<0.001\", \"Weak\"]\n          - [\"OLMo-2-1B\", -0.22, \"<0.001\", \"Weak\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2: Per-generator LOGO F1 bar chart with 95% CI error bars. Clear bimodal pattern: Pythia family (0.78-0.80) vs non-Pythia (0.57-0.62). CI bars for OLMo/Qwen overlap with 0.50 random baseline lower bound.\"\n      - \"Fig 3: entropy_mean trend lines (depth 0-4) for each generator. Pythia lines steep and parallel; OLMo nearly flat; Qwen shows weak inconsistent slope. Visual evidence of architecture-conditional response.\"\n    analysis: \"Universality claim collapses. The 2-tier pattern (Pythia strong, others weak) indicates depth signal is not an intrinsic property of recursive generation but depends on architecture/training-data alignment with the reference model AND possibly on the generator's own sampling dynamics. Two interpretations: (A) reference model mismatch — Pythia-410M is a poor scorer for non-Pythia text, inflating entropy baseline and suppressing drift measurement; (B) genuine architecture difference — some models produce more uniform token distributions at every depth, compressing the dynamic range for drift detection. Plan_003 (cross-family reference) will disambiguate. If (A), using OLMo/Qwen reference fixes it; if (B), the signal genuinely doesn't exist for these families. In worst tier, we expect (B) to dominate. Narrative must pivot to conditional claims.\"\n\n  - name: \"paraphrastic_comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Paraphrasing chains vs continuation chains 直接对比，测试 attractor convergence 理论\"\n    expected_results:\n      paraphrastic_3class_f1: 0.60\n      paraphrastic_binary_f1: 0.53\n      continuation_3class_f1: 0.72\n      continuation_binary_f1: 0.67\n      f1_3class_delta: -0.12\n      spearman_entropy_mean_para: 0.15\n      spearman_entropy_mean_cont: -0.42\n      spearman_ttr_para: 0.31\n      spearman_ttr_cont: -0.48\n      spearman_hapax_para: 0.28\n      spearman_hapax_cont: -0.51\n      cross_transfer_para_to_cont_f1: 0.38\n      cross_transfer_cont_to_para_f1: 0.42\n      depth_retention_para: 0.92\n      depth_retention_cont: 0.83\n      para_attractor_convergence_gen3: true\n      n_paraphrastic: 4800\n      n_continuation: 4600\n    result_rationale: \"Worst 档下，paraphrastic chains 呈现 attractor convergence 预期行为：entropy_mean Spearman 仅 +0.15（趋于 neutral/轻微 positive，即 paraphrasing 使 perplexity 略微上升后稳定）。但 continuation chains 也弱于 expected——在 5-gen pooled data 上 Spearman 仅 -0.42（而非 best 档的 -0.65+），因为 non-Pythia generators 拉低了整体 correlation。关键是 sign reversal：paraphrastic 正相关 vs continuation 负相关，但 effect size 都不大。Cross-transfer F1 极低（0.38-0.42），说明两种 chain 类型的 feature space 几乎不重叠——这在 worst 档是问题而非 feature，因为它意味着 'depth signal' 高度 task-specific，不是一个 unified phenomenon。Depth retention 0.92 for para（高于 continuation 的 0.83）也 counterintuitive：paraphrasing 保留更多 chains 但 signal 更弱，说明 chain stability ≠ signal strength。Attractor convergence 在 gen-3 后明显——para chains 的 feature 分布停止变化。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Paraphrastic vs Continuation Depth Signal\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Paraphrastic\", \"Continuation\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"3-class LOGO F1\", 0.60, 0.72, -0.12]\n          - [\"Binary LOGO F1\", 0.53, 0.67, -0.14]\n          - [\"ρ(entropy_mean, depth)\", \"+0.15\", \"-0.42\", \"sign reversed\"]\n          - [\"ρ(TTR, depth)\", \"+0.31\", \"-0.48\", \"sign reversed\"]\n          - [\"ρ(hapax, depth)\", \"+0.28\", \"-0.51\", \"sign reversed\"]\n          - [\"Depth retention (gen4/gen0)\", 0.92, 0.83, \"+0.09\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-transfer LOGO F1\"\n        columns: [\"Train on\", \"Test on\", \"F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Continuation\", \"Continuation\", 0.72]\n          - [\"Paraphrastic\", \"Paraphrastic\", 0.60]\n          - [\"Continuation → Para\", \"Paraphrastic\", 0.42]\n          - [\"Para → Continuation\", \"Continuation\", 0.38]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: Parallel feature trajectories (depth 0-4) for para vs cont chains. Continuation lines drift downward (vocabulary impoverishment); paraphrastic lines converge to plateau by gen-3 (attractor behavior). 但两者 effect sizes 都小于 expected。\"\n    analysis: \"Sign reversal confirms theoretically expected behavior (paraphrasing → attractor convergence, continuation → monotonic drift), but under worst tier the effect sizes are underwhelming for both types. Paraphrastic binary F1=0.53 is near random — essentially unclassifiable beyond gen-0 vs rest. Continuation is better but still weak (0.67 binary). The low cross-transfer (0.38-0.42) means there's no unified 'depth signal' that works across chain types — each requires its own model. For EMNLP reframing: this SUPPORTS the 'architecture-conditional' narrative because it shows depth signal properties depend on the specific generation process (paraphrasing vs continuation vs architecture), not just depth itself. The attractor convergence finding is a positive contribution to theory validation even in worst case.\"\n\n  - name: \"finer_grained_ordinal\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"5-class ordinal classification (gen-0 through gen-4) 测试更细粒度深度估计\"\n    expected_results:\n      5class_macro_f1: 0.38\n      5class_f1_std: 0.04\n      5class_accuracy: 0.42\n      5class_mae: 0.95\n      3class_macro_f1: 0.72\n      delta_5class_vs_3class: -0.34\n      per_class_f1:\n        depth_0: 0.85\n        depth_1: 0.45\n        depth_2: 0.22\n        depth_3: 0.18\n        depth_4: 0.20\n      confusion_concentration: \"gen2/gen3/gen4 互相混淆，占 confusion matrix off-diagonal 的 72%\"\n      ordinal_methods:\n        CORAL: 0.36\n        frank_hall: 0.39\n        xgboost: 0.38\n      depth_2_3_separability: \"Cohen's d = 0.08 (entropy_mean), 0.12 (hapax_ratio) — 几乎不可分\"\n      per_family_5class:\n        pythia_held_out: 0.48\n        olmo_held_out: 0.28\n        qwen_held_out: 0.31\n    result_rationale: \"Worst 档下，5-class 在 pooled 5-gen data 上 macro F1 仅 0.38，接近 5-class random baseline（0.20）但仍显著高于 chance。核心问题：depth 2/3/4 几乎不可分（per-class F1 0.18-0.22）。原因是双重的：(1) depth drift 在多数生成器（OLMo/Qwen）上本身就弱，加上 (2) gen-2 到 gen-4 之间的 feature 增量极小（Cohen's d < 0.12），即使在 Pythia 上也进入 plateau。只有 gen-0 可靠分类（F1=0.85），gen-1 中等（0.45）——这本质上是 binary detection（gen-0 vs rest）在 5-class 框架中的残影。OLMo/Qwen held-out 时 5-class F1 掉到 0.28-0.31（接近 random），进一步说明 fine-grained 深度估计只在特定架构下可行。Ordinal-specific methods（CORAL/Frank-Hall）无优势，因为 underlying signal 本身不存在于 deep depths。3-class（0.72）远优于 5-class（0.38），但 delta = 34pp 说明 3-class 的性能也主要来自 gen-0 classification 而非真正的 ordinal discrimination。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Ordinal Classification Results\"\n        columns: [\"Granularity\", \"Method\", \"Macro F1\", \"MAE\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"3-class\", \"XGBoost\", 0.72, 0.31]\n          - [\"5-class\", \"XGBoost\", 0.38, 0.95]\n          - [\"5-class\", \"CORAL\", 0.36, 0.98]\n          - [\"5-class\", \"Frank-Hall\", 0.39, 0.92]\n      - name: \"Table: 5-class Per-depth F1\"\n        columns: [\"Depth\", \"F1\", \"Support\", \"Most confused with\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"gen-0\", 0.85, 4950, \"gen-1 (10%)\"]\n          - [\"gen-1\", 0.45, 4900, \"gen-2 (28%)\"]\n          - [\"gen-2\", 0.22, 4600, \"gen-3 (35%), gen-1 (22%)\"]\n          - [\"gen-3\", 0.18, 4200, \"gen-2 (33%), gen-4 (30%)\"]\n          - [\"gen-4\", 0.20, 3800, \"gen-3 (38%), gen-2 (21%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: 5×5 Confusion matrix heatmap。gen-0 行几乎全在对角线；gen-2/3/4 行呈均匀分布，对角线无明显 peak。直观展示 depth > 1 的不可分性。\"\n      - \"Fig 6: Feature distributions (violin plots) by depth 0-4, split by generator family。Pythia violins 逐层分离；OLMo/Qwen violins 从 depth-1 开始完全重叠。\"\n    analysis: \"5-class ordinal is infeasible in worst tier. The signal exists primarily at the gen-0/gen-1 boundary and rapidly degrades. This is actually informative for the reframed paper: it establishes an empirical ceiling on depth resolution (≤3 classes) that's architecture-dependent. For Pythia-family generators where signal is strong, 4-class might work; for others, even binary (gen-1 vs gen-2+) is near chance. The 'conditions under which depth signal emerges vs collapses' framing gains direct evidence: depth granularity is architecture-conditional, not a universal property of recursive generation. Report as structured negative finding.\"\n\n  - name: \"end_to_end_classifier\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"QLoRA fine-tuned Qwen3.5-0.8B 端到端深度分类，对比 handcrafted features\"\n    expected_results:\n      5class_macro_f1: 0.44\n      5class_f1_std: 0.02\n      3class_macro_f1: 0.76\n      3class_f1_std: 0.01\n      per_class_f1:\n        gen0: 0.95\n        gen1: 0.62\n        gen2: 0.30\n        gen3: 0.22\n        gen4: 0.11\n      vs_xgboost_5class_delta_pp: \"+6.0\"\n      vs_xgboost_3class_delta_pp: \"+4.0\"\n      logo_generalization:\n        pythia_held_out: 0.52\n        olmo_held_out: 0.35\n        qwen_held_out: 0.38\n      overfitting_gap: 0.18\n      train_f1: 0.62\n      val_f1: 0.44\n      runtime_hours: 14\n      model: \"Qwen3-0.6B-Base\"\n      method: \"QLoRA rank-16\"\n    result_rationale: \"E2E model 在 5-class 上优于 XGBoost（0.44 vs 0.38，+6pp），因为 learned representations 能捕获 handcrafted features 遗漏的 subtle patterns（如 attention pattern shifts、specific n-gram frequency changes）。但绝对性能仍然很差（0.44），且 overfitting 严重（train 0.62 vs val 0.44，gap=18pp）——模型学到了 generator-specific artifacts 而非 generalizable depth signal。LOGO generalization 更加灾难性：held-out Pythia F1=0.52，OLMo/Qwen 仅 0.35-0.38。这说明 E2E model 学到的不是 'depth signal' 而是 'generator fingerprint + depth 交互'——它在训练集内的 generator 上过拟合。3-class（0.76）优于 XGBoost（0.72）但差距不大（+4pp），且同样来自 gen-0 classification。在 worst 档下，E2E 的相对优势说明确实有 beyond-handcrafted-features 的信号存在，但这些信号 generator-specific、不泛化，支持 'architecture-conditional' reframing。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: E2E vs Handcrafted Features\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"5-class F1\", \"3-class F1\", \"LOGO 5-class F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"XGBoost 7-feature\", 0.38, 0.72, 0.34]\n          - [\"QLoRA Qwen3-0.6B\", 0.44, 0.76, 0.38]\n          - [\"Delta\", \"+0.06\", \"+0.04\", \"+0.04\"]\n      - name: \"Table: QLoRA LOGO Per-family Held-out\"\n        columns: [\"Held-out Family\", \"5-class F1\", \"Overfitting gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pythia (2.8B+1B)\", 0.52, 0.10]\n          - [\"OLMo-2-1B\", 0.35, 0.27]\n          - [\"Qwen (1.7B+0.6B)\", 0.38, 0.24]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: Learning curves (train/val F1 vs epoch). Val F1 plateaus at epoch 3 while train continues climbing → clear overfitting signal. Val F1 on held-out families (OLMo/Qwen) peaks at epoch 2 then degrades.\"\n    analysis: \"E2E model provides modest improvement over handcrafted features but does not solve the fundamental problem: depth signal for non-Pythia architectures is weak or absent. The overfitting pattern (generator-specific memorization) is actually diagnostic evidence for the reframed paper: it shows that whatever distinguishes depths for a given generator is not transferable across architectures. This supports the 'architecture-conditional depth response' thesis — each model family has its own depth signature (if any), and there is no universal learned representation of 'depth'. For the paper: report as supplementary evidence that neither handcrafted nor learned features achieve universal depth discrimination, strengthening the conditional-claim reframing.\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6b710055-31f3-4d1c-83bc-cef72e560573","total_cost_usd":0.43446199999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28762,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":8998,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28762,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8998,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28762},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":23724,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.023819,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":8998,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28762,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.410643,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"78257cf2-f2dd-42cb-a48f-2eeda8d9bda4"}
